<h1>Lazy loading of the deferred renderers</h1>

<p>
  Two deferred blocks — a <code>mermaid</code> fence and a <code>math</code>
  fence — placed deliberately far below the fold, and far apart from each other,
  so each library fetch is attributable to the block that scrolled into view.
  None of this is stubbed: <code>mermaid</code> and <code>katex</code> are
  pinned in the host's importmap, with no preload.
</p>

<p>
  Compare with <a href="/harness">/harness</a>, which has no deferred block at
  all and must therefore request neither library.
</p>

